# Supabase — public client configuration.
#
# Both values below are public by design: they are compiled into the browser
# bundle on every build, so they are already visible to anyone who loads the
# site. What actually protects your data is Row Level Security on each table
# (see docs/SUPABASE.md) — not the secrecy of this key.
#
# Environment variables set in the hosting platform (Vercel: Project Settings →
# Environment Variables) override this file, which is the better home for them
# if you would rather they not live in the repository.
#
# NEVER put the service_role key here. It bypasses RLS and this file is
# committed.

# This is also the hostname Google shows on its sign-in sheet ("to continue to
# …"). To put your own name there instead, follow docs/AUTH-DOMAIN.md and change
# this one value to https://auth.quickstark.tech — nothing in the code hardcodes
# the Supabase host, so that is the whole change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://esuatccbicekcohzgcvd.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImVzdWF0Y2NiaWNla2NvaHpnY3ZkIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODc4Nzg5MTQsImV4cCI6MjEwMzQ1NDkxNH0.vIHvaQzdgin0eq2o2PEdLbIfOYKBUTi1rPbgp4OgrVw

# ── Crypto checkout — the wallet payments are collected in ────────────────────
#
# Public by design, like the two values above: this address is printed on the
# payment screen and encoded into the QR code, so every customer sees it. It is
# a receiving address, and a receiving address is meant to be given out.
#
# It is here rather than only in the hosting environment so that a deploy picks
# it up with no dashboard step. Two consequences worth knowing:
#
#   - It is a public record. Anyone reading this repository, and anyone who
#     buys credits, can look this address up on a block explorer and see its
#     balance and every payment it has ever received.
#   - Moving to a different wallet is a commit and a deploy. Setting
#     CRYPTO_WALLET_BTC in Vercel overrides this line without one.
#
# Verified before it was written here: 25 decoded bytes, version 0x00,
# Base58Check checksum 11ad15eb. `npm run check:payments` re-checks it.
CRYPTO_WALLET_BTC=1FWzCzC4vQsnXJmTb3wfxWinyDKX6rh4t2

# The two values the checkout still needs are secrets and must NOT be added to
# this file — it is committed. Set them in Vercel → Environment Variables:
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY       — without it, pressing Pay fails: orders
#                                     cannot be written from a browser.
#   CRYPTO_PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_SECRET  — without it, no settlement call is
#                                     accepted. Payments can still be settled by
#                                     hand from the Supabase SQL editor; see
#                                     "Settling without a webhook" in
#                                     docs/PAYMENTS.md.
